Yes, the argument trim=TRUE does exactly this:
ggplot(mtcars)+
  geom_point(aes(y=mpg, x=wt,col=factor(cyl)))+
  geom_density(aes(x=wt,y=..scaled..*30,col=factor(cyl)), trim=TRUE)

This is documented in ?stat_density.
​

